.TH QUICKSILVER-VAULT "1" "September 2026" "quicksilver-vault v0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quicksilver-vault \- manual page for quicksilver-vault v0.1.0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quicksilver-vault
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,<command>\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
quicksilver\-vault version v0.1.0
.PP
quicksilver\-vault is an offline tool for creating and interacting with Quicksilver vault files.
.PP
By default quicksilver\-vault will act on vaults in the default mainnet vault directory in the datadir.
.PP
To change the target vault, use the \fB\-datadir\fR, \fB\-vault\fR and (test)chain selection arguments.
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\fB\-datadir=\fR<dir>
.IP
Specify data directory
.HP
\fB\-dumpfile=\fR<file name>
.IP
When used with 'dump', writes out the records to this file. When used
with 'createfromdump', loads the records into a new vault.
.HP
\fB\-format=\fR<format>
.IP
The format of the vault file to create. Only "sqlite" is supported. Only
used with 'createfromdump'
.HP
\fB\-help\fR
.IP
Print this help message and exit (also \fB\-h\fR or \-?)
.HP
\fB\-vault=\fR<vault\-name>
.IP
Specify vault name
.HP
\fB\-version\fR
.IP
Print version and exit
.PP
Debugging/Testing options:
.HP
\fB\-debug=\fR<category>
.IP
Output debugging information (default: 0).
.HP
\fB\-printtoconsole\fR
.IP
Send trace/debug info to console (default: 1 when no \fB\-debug\fR is true, 0
otherwise).
.PP
Chain selection options:
.HP
\fB\-chain=\fR<chain>
.IP
Use the chain <chain> (default: main). Allowed values: main, publictest,
sandbox
.HP
\fB\-publictest\fR
.IP
Use the Quicksilver Public Test Network. Equivalent to
\fB\-chain\fR=\fI\,publictest\/\fR.
.PP
Commands:
.IP
create
.IP
Create new vault file
.IP
createfromdump
.IP
Create new vault file from dumped records
.IP
dump
.IP
Print out all of the vault key\-value records
.IP
info
.IP
Get vault info
